globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN=Object.assign(globalThis.STORY_ZW_PAL_EN||{},{
'遷移':{
'紫微':{title:`An honored guest with a business card in hand`,story:`With Zi Wei in your Travel palace, you carry more weight out in the world than you do at home. People take you for someone reliable and well placed, and influential people often give you a hand up. Building your life away from home and dealing with the outside world tends to open more doors than staying put. The lesson: you may keep up such a polished front outside that you only feel the fatigue once you get home, and caring about your image can stop you from asking for help.`,scenes:[`Say you travel to an unfamiliar city for work and meet a client for the first time, and they introduce you to their boss without being asked.`,`You might be gracious and attentive all day in public, then get home and not want to answer a single message.`],advice:`Out in the world, leave yourself room to say "I don't really know this one." Helpful people find it easier to come closer.`},
'紫微·天府':{title:`Heading out with two sets of keys`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tian Fu together in your Travel palace, you come across as steady and well resourced, and resources and contacts tend to gather around you. Big cities, large organizations and stages that span regions are big enough for you. The blind spot: away from home you care a lot about safety and appearances, so when a new opportunity shows up you tend to tally the risks first and end up a step behind.`,scenes:[`Say you move somewhere new for work. You quickly figure out which bank, which agent and which senior colleague you can trust.`,`You might always book a well-reviewed hotel when traveling, happy to skip a sight if it means sleeping soundly.`],advice:`When an opportunity comes up somewhere else, set a limit you can live with if it goes wrong, then let yourself try it once.`},
'紫微·天相':{title:`The mediator who shows up in a suit`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tian Xiang in your Travel palace, you get along well with people and present a proper image, so you are often asked to be the go-between or the representative. Out in the world you follow the rules and keep your word, which earns you help from within the system and the trust of people higher up. The lesson: you care a great deal about how others see you, and one comment from outside can stay with you for days.`,scenes:[`Say your department needs someone to negotiate a partnership with another company. You are the first name everyone thinks of.`,`You might rehearse your toast three times the night before a friend's wedding.`],advice:`Swap "What will people think?" for "What does this situation need?" and your decisions will come more easily.`},
'紫微·破軍':{title:`The pioneer who wants to redraw the route`,story:`With Zi Wei and Po Jun in your Travel palace, the world outside keeps shifting, and you are good at breaking new ground in other places or new fields. People see you as bold and willing to charge ahead, and you are often handed jobs that need a full rebuild. The lesson: outside events change a lot, your plans get disrupted often, and the urge to move somewhere new runs strong.`,scenes:[`Say you are sent to take over a chaotic branch office. Within three months you have rebuilt its whole workflow.`,`You might change your travel plans halfway through to visit a small town you had never planned on, and it turns out to be the part you remember most.`],advice:`Before each move, write down what you want to take with you and what you want to leave behind. That way every change adds to your strength.`},
'紫微·七殺':{title:`A general who can hold ground alone`,story:`With Zi Wei and Qi Sha in your Travel palace, you carry authority and make decisions quickly, so people readily hand you heavy responsibilities. You get plenty of chances to work away from home and run things on your own, and the less familiar the place, the more it brings out your ability. The lesson: there is a lot of pressure out there, you are used to just pushing through, and you can come across as hard to approach.`,scenes:[`Say you are posted to a new market. You visit clients and negotiate terms on your own, and within six months the numbers are up.`,`You might skip the small talk at a party full of strangers and go straight to the host to talk business.`],advice:`Find one or two partners out there you can be honest with. Running the show doesn't mean carrying it all by yourself.`},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:`Bringing your own spotlight to every party`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tan Lang in your Travel palace, you are socially skilled and never short of things to talk about. You draw people in, and you often meet influential people at dinners, parties and nights out. The world outside is exciting, and full of temptation too. The lesson: if you let loose too much, time and money quietly drain away, and you need to keep business favors and romance clearly separate.`,scenes:[`Say you strike up a conversation with the next table at a friend's birthday party, and that person later becomes a business partner.`,`You might come back from a work trip with an expense report that is half dinners and after-parties.`],advice:`Before you head out, decide what this gathering is for. Have a great time, and bring something useful home too.`},
'天機':{title:`A traveler with a map who still loves the back roads`,story:`With Tian Ji in your Travel palace, your mind works fast and you adapt quickly when you are out and about. You suit settings that call for flexibility, information and planning, and good ideas often come to you while you are on the move. {{B:天機:In a strong position, your quick wits are enough to catch the chances that come your way.|In a weak position, you may overthink and rush around a lot for little return.}} The lesson: your plans change often, and others may feel you aren't settled enough.`,scenes:[`Say you take a ninety-minute train ride for work and rethink the structure of your whole proposal along the way.`,`You might change your commute twice in a year just because you found a route that saves five minutes.`],advice:`Jot down the ideas that pop up while you are out. Back at your desk, pick one and finish it before moving on to the next.`},
'天機·太陰':{title:`A careful strategist moving by moonlight`,story:`With Tian Ji and Tai Yin in your Travel palace, you are perceptive and pay close attention to detail when you are out in the world, and help often comes from women or from gentle people. You do well in work that earns through movement or depends on planning and detail, and moves, work trips and changes of scene come up often. The lesson: your mood is easily swayed by your surroundings, and a new place makes you uneasy for a while.`,scenes:[`Say you move to a new city. You only relax after you have walked past the nearby grocery store, clinic and café.`,`You might get homesick easily on the road and lie on the hotel bed at night scrolling through old photos.`],advice:`Give yourself time to adjust to a new place. Don't decide in the first week whether it's good or bad.`},
'天機·巨門':{title:`An analyst who makes their way with words`,story:`With Tian Ji and Ju Men in your Travel palace, you speak well and analyze sharply, and you are suited to opening doors in new places through expertise and communication, for example as a consultant, trainer, salesperson or researcher. There is a lot of information out there, and you are good at sorting it. The lesson: you can get pulled into gossip and disputes, and speaking too bluntly or too fast can get you misunderstood.`,scenes:[`Say you ask a question at a conference and point out a gap the speaker hadn't considered. Afterward, lots of people come over to swap business cards.`,`You might hear every kind of rumor in your first month at a new company and have trouble telling which ones to believe.`],advice:`Out in the world, listen to three sentences before you say one. Your analysis will carry more weight and cause fewer misunderstandings.`},
'天機·天梁':{title:`The adviser on the road`,story:`With Tian Ji and Tian Liang in your Travel palace, you are often the one who comes up with the plan, and people think of you when they have a problem. You get along with older people and tend to meet mentors willing to guide you, and you suit work away from home that involves expert judgment, planning or education. The lesson: people out there talk a lot and act little, and you too may think much more than you do.`,scenes:[`Say a friend is about to go abroad and calls you first to ask which travel insurance or credit card is the better deal.`,`You might meet a retired professional at a workshop and then take them to dinner once a year to ask their advice.`],advice:`While you are giving others advice, pick one thing for yourself and start on it right away.`},
'太陽':{title:`A sun that shines wherever it goes`,story:`With Tai Yang in your Travel palace, you are warm, generous and ready to pitch in when you are out in the world, and people notice you easily. You do well away from home, in public settings and in work that puts you in front of people. {{B:太陽:In a strong position, reputation and support come to you quickly.|In a weak position, you give a lot and the rewards come slowly, and your warmth isn't always returned.}} The lesson: you spend too much energy out there.`,scenes:[`Say a colleague is moving house. You are the first to say "I have a car, I'll help," and your whole weekend disappears.`,`You might volunteer to host an event, then get home so tired you don't want to talk.`],advice:`Before you pitch in, ask yourself whether you actually want to this time. Let your warmth be a choice, not a habit.`},
'太陽·太陰':{title:`A traveler with two faces, sun and moon`,story:`With Tai Yang and Tai Yin in your Travel palace, you are warm and outgoing at some moments and reserved at others, switching naturally to suit the setting. Help may come from both men and women, and work that spans regions, runs on shifts or turns day into night is common for you. The lesson: your moods swing more when you are out, hot one moment and cool the next, which leaves people unsure what you are thinking.`,scenes:[`Say you talk confidently through meetings all day, then sit alone in your hotel room late into the night quietly sorting your notes.`,`On a trip you might want a lively night market one minute and a quiet bookshop the next.`],advice:`Keep an eye on your battery when you are out. When it runs low, say so instead of forcing the cheer.`},
'太陽·巨門':{title:`Heard out in the world through your voice`,story:`With Tai Yang and Ju Men in your Travel palace, you do well away from home through speaking, teaching, media or sales, and the more public the stage, the more opportunity you find. People see you as frank and persuasive. The lesson: there is plenty of talk out there, and even well-meant honesty can be taken as criticism. When Tai Yang is bright, disputes are easier to settle.`,scenes:[`Say you give a presentation to a client, clear and warm, and they tell you on the spot, "We'll sign next week."`,`You might post a frank suggestion in a group chat and have it read as an attack on someone.`],advice:`Before you say something hard, say what you care about. People take it in more easily.`},
'太陽·天梁':{title:`Treated like the big brother or sister as soon as you step out`,story:`With Tai Yang and Tian Liang in your Travel palace, you get on well with elders and attract helpful people, and you often end up looking after others. You suit work away from home in public service, education, healthcare, large organizations or charities, and a good reputation builds easily. The lesson: you take charge of too much, kindness turns into obligation, and you often give more than you get back.`,scenes:[`Say you go on a group trip and somehow become the one who splits the bills, finds the way and calls the taxis.`,`You might spend your first weeks at a new job solving the new hires' problems and end up writing your own report at midnight.`],advice:`Before you help, check what the other person actually wants. Looking after others should still leave energy for you.`},
'武曲':{title:`A doer who heads out with a calculator`,story:`With Wu Qu in your Travel palace, you work briskly and care about efficiency out in the world. You suit work away from home or in business settings, and the more you move, the more you earn. People see you as practical and dependable, someone who doesn't waste words. The lesson: you can be too rigid out there, talking only about results, which can make you seem cold.`,scenes:[`Say you are on a business trip to discuss a deal. While the other side is still making small talk, you already have the quote and the timeline on the table.`,`You might log every coffee on a trip and make a spending chart when you get back.`],advice:`Leave five minutes for chat before getting down to business. Goodwill is a kind of capital too.`},
'武曲·天府':{title:`Guarding the granary even far from home`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tian Fu in your Travel palace, you manage money well and keep a stable network wherever you go. You suit running a business or managing assets away from home, or working in finance and commerce, and people trust you with money and resources. The lesson: you play it safe out there and rarely take risks, and your relationships can start to feel too much like transactions.`,scenes:[`Say a group of friends pools money for an event. Everyone wants you to keep the books, because you even sort the receipts.`,`Before a trip abroad you might research where to get the best exchange rate more carefully than the sights.`],advice:`Keep part of your budget for experiences. The world out there is worth spending a little on without keeping count.`},
'武曲·天相':{title:`A trusted executive away from home`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tian Xiang in your Travel palace, you keep your word and take responsibility out in the world, which earns the trust of partners and superiors. You suit work away from home in finance, administration, contracts or management. The lesson: you take on too much of other people's business, and when you are stuck in the middle trying to broker a deal, you can end up pleasing no one.`,scenes:[`Say two departments are fighting over budget, and in the end you are the one called into the meeting room to mediate.`,`You might cover a friend's share of a trip and still have to ask for it back six months later.`],advice:`When you help with other people's money, set the rules clearly first. That is how goodwill lasts.`},
'武曲·七殺':{title:`A warrior charging ahead out in the world`,story:`With Wu Qu and Qi Sha in your Travel palace, you have plenty of drive and act fast. You suit working away from home, starting a business or jobs judged on results, and people see you as tough and willing to fight for it. The lesson: the outside world changes a lot and the pressure is high, so when you are in a hurry you can make rash decisions. When you are constantly on the road, watch your safety and your fatigue.`,scenes:[`Say you land a project in another city. You book your ticket the same day and are on site the next morning.`,`You might travel for three weeks straight to close a deal, then come home to find everything in the fridge has expired.`],advice:`Before each charge, set aside a day to get organized. You can have speed and stability together.`},
'武曲·破軍':{title:`An adventurer who dares to start over somewhere new`,story:`With Wu Qu and Po Jun in your Travel palace, life away from home brings many changes and big ups and downs. You suit going out to try your luck elsewhere or switching tracks, and you build your strength by starting over again and again. People see you as someone who spends boldly and works boldly. The lesson: out in the world, money comes in fast and goes out fast, so think one step further before an impulse purchase or an impulsive commitment.`,scenes:[`Say you fall in love with a city on a trip, and three months later you really do apply for a transfer there.`,`On work trips you might buy something you like without comparing prices.`],advice:`Before a big decision somewhere new, set aside living expenses you won't touch. Then your risk has a safety net.`},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:`A businessperson who grows stronger with time away`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tan Lang in your Travel palace, you have a head for business and a talent for socializing, and you suit trading away from home, sales or entertainment. This pair is often said to be hard at first and easier later: early years away from home are tougher, and things take off once you have built up enough. The lesson: there is a lot of entertaining and a lot of wanting out there, so tell investments apart from indulgence.`,scenes:[`Say you work in sales in another city. The first two years are a slog, and in the third year clients start referring new clients to you.`,`You might come up with a side business over drinks with friends and register it the following week.`],advice:`Give yourself a five-year window. Don't give up on an opportunity away from home just because the first year or two are slow.`},
'天同':{title:`Finding a comfortable corner wherever you go`,story:`With Tian Tong in your Travel palace, you are easygoing and well liked out in the world, people tend to look after you, and you know how to enjoy the moment. {{B:天同:In a strong position, life away from home is relaxed and blessed.|In a weak position, you may lack drive and let your surroundings push you along.}} The lesson: you seek too much comfort out there and want to hide when pressure comes.`,scenes:[`Say you travel to an unfamiliar city for work. You find a good breakfast spot first, and by the next day the owner remembers your order.`,`If you get a difficult boss at a new job, your first thought might be to switch teams rather than talk it out.`],advice:`When something uncomfortable happens out there, try to get through it once. You will find you can handle more pressure than you thought.`},
'天同·太陰':{title:`A gentle traveler with good taste`,story:`With Tian Tong and Tai Yin in your Travel palace, you are mild, perceptive and have an eye for beauty, and help often comes from women and gentle people. You suit work away from home connected to lifestyle, aesthetics or service. The lesson: you are emotionally sensitive out there and take any coolness to heart, and fear of conflict can make you put up with things you shouldn't.`,scenes:[`Say you travel and remember which guesthouse had the nicest-smelling sheets and which street had the prettiest lights.`,`A new colleague might answer you coldly, and you spend the whole evening wondering what you did wrong.`],advice:`Out in the world, say "I need" out loud. Gentle people deserve to be treated well too.`},
'天同·巨門':{title:`Smiling out the door, sighing once home`,story:`With Tian Tong and Ju Men in your Travel palace, you seem easygoing out in the world, but inside you think a lot. With people you can run into misunderstandings, communication gaps, or end up quietly losing out. The upside is that you know how to defuse things with humor, and you suit work built on speaking, service or communication. The lesson: you don't speak up in the moment, then keep turning it over in your head afterward.`,scenes:[`Say a colleague asks you to cover a shift. You agree with a smile, then get home wondering whether they are taking you for granted.`,`You might spend half a day of a trip giving your travel companion the silent treatment over a small mix-up about the itinerary.`],advice:`When something bothers you, say a light sentence about it right then. It takes far less energy than replaying it a hundred times later.`},
'天同·天梁':{title:`A lucky star who always has backup out in the world`,story:`With Tian Tong and Tian Liang in your Travel palace, you have helpful people and good rapport with elders, and someone often happens to help just when you need it. People see you as kind and dependable, and you suit charity, education, healthcare and service work. The lesson: you can lean too much on outside help and lack the grit to fight for things yourself, and you soften easily out there.`,scenes:[`Say you lose your passport abroad and happen to meet a kind fellow traveler from home who takes you to the consulate to replace it.`,`In a new place, senior colleagues might often treat you to dinner while you still haven't decided where you want to go.`],advice:`When luck is on your side, also set yourself a goal you will reach on your own.`},
'廉貞':{title:`Knowing the rules and knowing people`,story:`With Lian Zhen in your Travel palace, you are socially skilled out in the world, read situations well and know where the lines are. You suit growing within a system, in public relations, management or a specialist field, and people see you as charming with clear boundaries. The lesson: you carry a lot in your head out there, going along on the surface while making your own calculations, and you can get drawn into power struggles.`,scenes:[`Say you are at a company dinner. You always remember which manager doesn't drink and which one likes a compliment.`,`You might notice two camps in a new team and spend weeks agonizing over whether to pick a side.`],advice:`Out in the world, hold on to your principles. Be flexible with people, but don't let your bottom line change with the setting.`},
'廉貞·天府':{title:`Heading out with rules and supplies`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tian Fu in your Travel palace, you are steady and rule-abiding out in the world, and you know how to cultivate contacts and resources. You suit management, administration, finance or large organizations away from home, and people trust your judgment. The lesson: you are too cautious out there, used to playing it safe, so you react a beat late when opportunity comes.`,scenes:[`Say you are about to be posted elsewhere. You research local rents, transport and regulations and put it all in a spreadsheet first.`,`You might not say much at gatherings, but whenever you recommend someone, your manager takes it seriously.`],advice:`Give yourself more room to improvise out there. Not everything needs to be fully prepared before you begin.`},
'廉貞·天相':{title:`A steady representative at formal occasions`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tian Xiang in your Travel palace, you know how to handle the world and care about image and rules. You suit work as a representative, coordinator, or in PR, law or administration, and people see you as polished and tactful. The lesson: you clean up too many things for others out there, or get pulled between the rules and personal ties, which wears you out.`,scenes:[`Say your company is signing a contract with an office in another city, and your manager puts you in charge of the details.`,`You might get roped into handling the gift table at a friend's wedding and not eat anything all evening.`],advice:`Before you agree to help, ask yourself whether you have the energy. Being gracious includes taking care of yourself.`},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:`Cutting a path through unfamiliar ground`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Qi Sha in your Travel palace, you have the drive to push forward out in the world and aren't afraid of difficulty. You suit pioneering in new places, sales, or work that needs tough execution, and people see you as forceful and opinionated. The lesson: the outside world changes a lot and conflicts are frequent, and when you meet force with force, both sides can get hurt. When you are often on the road, watch your safety.`,scenes:[`Say you are sent to fix a mess. In the first week you have a big argument with the other side, but things actually start moving.`,`You might drive long distances without taking breaks, finishing the whole trip in one go.`],advice:`Put your drive into the task and soften your tone with people. The road will open up wider.`},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:`A reformer who tears down and builds as they go`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Po Jun in your Travel palace, life out in the world changes often, you frequently start over because your surroundings shift, and you are good at finding opportunity in change. People see you as having strong character and daring to challenge the rules. The lesson: you easily clash with institutions or people out there, and decisions made on impulse often take effort to clean up afterward.`,scenes:[`Say you propose a major overhaul at a new company. Some people admire it, and some quietly resent it.`,`You might live in two different cities within a year and throw out half your things each time you move.`],advice:`When you want to break the old and build the new, find an ally to push with you. It's far steadier than forcing your way through alone.`},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:`In your element where things are lively`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tan Lang in your Travel palace, you are highly social and full of charm out in the world. You suit entertainment, sales, PR, food and drink, and other fields built on contacts. There are many opportunities out there, and many temptations. The lesson: socializing and romance can easily go too far, and if you misjudge the limits, trouble follows.`,scenes:[`Say you go to a brand event and add twenty new contacts in one night, and the following week someone gets in touch about working together.`,`You might fill every night of a trip abroad with bars and night markets, then need a week to recover once you're back.`],advice:`Before you head home, ask yourself: of all today's connections, which ones do I really want to keep?`},
'天府':{title:`Carrying a storehouse wherever you go`,story:`With Tian Fu in your Travel palace, you are steady and give off a sense of security out in the world, and resources and support tend to come to you. You suit management, running a business or large organizations away from home, and people see you as reliable and good at sharing things out. The lesson: you are conservative out there, focused on protecting what you already have, and slow to move in a completely new environment.`,scenes:[`Say you travel with friends. Your bag has everything, and whoever is missing a charging cable or a bandage comes to you.`,`If someone asks whether you'd move to a new branch, your first reaction might be "But what happens here then?"`],advice:`Now and then, travel light. You can get along fine without being fully prepared.`},
'太陰':{title:`A fine sensitivity that shows by moonlight`,story:`With Tai Yin in your Travel palace, you are gentle and attentive out in the world, and help often comes from women or kind people. You suit work away from home connected to night hours, service, aesthetics, finance or real estate. {{B:太陰:In a strong position, money and goodwill flow smoothly when you are out in the world.|In a weak position, you carry a lot on your mind, your moods rise and fall, and your efforts aren't easily seen.}} The lesson: you look after other people's feelings so much that you short-change yourself.`,scenes:[`Say you work in another city. It's often your landlady or a female colleague who looks out for you.`,`On a trip you might not mention a place you really want to visit, just so you don't inconvenience your companions.`],advice:`Put your own needs on the itinerary. Attentive people deserve to be looked after too.`},
'貪狼':{title:`The world outside is your playground`,story:`With Tan Lang in your Travel palace, you are highly social out in the world, with wide interests and the ability to adapt quickly. Opportunities often come at gatherings, on trips and at fun events, and people see you as entertaining, playful and multi-talented. If Tan Lang is in a strong position, these chances are more likely to turn into real gains. The lesson: there's a lot of temptation out there, so you may dabble in everything without going deep, and time and money go fast.`,scenes:[`Say you take a one-off pottery class and get talking with the teacher, which later turns into a collaboration.`,`You might sign up for three courses in one month and still be attending only one by the next.`],advice:`Pick one of your outside interests and go deep. Being multi-talented will become real skill.`},
'巨門':{title:`Letting your expertise speak out in the world`,story:`With Ju Men in your Travel palace, you suit earning a living away from home through speaking and expertise, for example in teaching, law, sales, consulting or media. You observe closely and ask probing questions. {{B:巨門:In a strong position, your way with words can turn into a good reputation.|In a weak position, disputes come up more often, so choose your words with extra care.}} The lesson: there is a lot of talk out there, and you can be misunderstood or become the target of false rumors.`,scenes:[`Say the first time you speak up at a new workplace, you point out a flaw in the system. Some people are impressed, and some think you are nitpicking.`,`You might hear something you said being repeated back to you, only to find its meaning twisted.`],advice:`Keep a written record of important matters, so no one can rewrite what you said.`},
'天相':{title:`A trusted helper out in the world`,story:`With Tian Xiang in your Travel palace, you follow the rules and keep your word out in the world, so superiors and partners trust you easily, and helpful people often give you a boost. People see you as steady and courteous. The lesson: outside opinions sway you too easily, and you can get so busy doing things for others that you forget what you want.`,scenes:[`Say a new colleague can't figure out the expense process. Your manager says, "Ask them, they know it best."`,`You might want to leave a get-together early but stay until the very end because everyone else is still there.`],advice:`Practice saying "I'm heading off" when you are out. Being trusted doesn't depend on pushing yourself.`},
'天梁':{title:`An elder holding an umbrella over you when you step out`,story:`With Tian Liang in your Travel palace, you have protection out in the world. You often meet elders or mentors willing to help you, and trouble tends to resolve itself. People see you as mature and reasonable, and you are often asked to judge right from wrong. The lesson: you like to get involved in other people's business out there, and your good intentions can come across as lecturing. Because someone is always there to help, you may also neglect what you should be carrying yourself.`,scenes:[`Say you get lost abroad. There always seems to be a local old man who walks over and shows you part of the way.`,`You might see a colleague make a mistake and can't help pointing it out, only for them to feel scolded.`],advice:`Before giving advice, ask "Would you like to hear what I think?" Then your good intentions will land.`},
'七殺':{title:`Brave enough to travel far on your own`,story:`With Qi Sha in your Travel palace, you are independent and decisive out in the world, and unfamiliar, difficult environments bring out the best in you. You suit working away from home, starting a business, sales, or breaking new ground, and people see you as commanding. The lesson: life out there changes a lot and the travel is tiring. When you move too fast, watch your safety, and don't let your forcefulness scare off people who want to help.`,scenes:[`Say you go backpacking alone. Where you don't speak the language, you get things done with gestures.`,`You might volunteer for the most difficult client in your first month at a new company.`],advice:`When you are working hard out there, give yourself regular days off. A long run takes you further than a sprint.`},
'破軍':{title:`Every trip out is a fresh start`,story:`With Po Jun in your Travel palace, life out in the world changes a lot, and you often start over because of a move, a new job or a new setting. Out there you dare to charge ahead and to change things, which suits work that creates something new or breaks the old pattern, and people see you as a bit rebellious and full of character. The lesson: the outside world drains you, you start many things, and wrapping them up takes effort.`,scenes:[`Say you have just joined a new department, and you redo the entire filing system your predecessor left behind.`,`You might always want to go places no one else goes when you travel, and your plans often change at the last minute.`],advice:`Before each new beginning, close out the last one properly. That's how you carry your experience forward.`},
'空':{title:`A mirror that changes color with its surroundings`,story:`Your Travel palace has no main star, so how you act out in the world is shaped by your surroundings and the people around you. You are very flexible and can grow into whatever a place calls for. This palace usually borrows the main stars from the opposite palace, your Life palace, so the gap between how you are outside and at home should be read together with your Life palace. The upside is strong adaptability; the lesson is that outside forces can easily pull you along and leave you unsure what you really want.`,scenes:[`Say you go out with lively friends and you are the life of the party, but with quiet people you can go all evening without talking.`,`You might change jobs and find your whole way of dressing and speaking changes with it.`],advice:`When you change settings, note which habits you chose for yourself. However much the outside world shifts, you will still have a core of your own.`}
},
'父母':{
'紫微':{title:`A dignified ruler sitting above you`,story:`With Zi Wei in your Parents palace, the elders, bosses and people who raised you are often opinionated and commanding. They may give you resources and a broader view, and they may also set high demands and rarely let you decide. You usually get along well with institutions, paperwork and exams, and people in high positions tend to promote you. The lesson: in front of authority you are used to going along first and rebelling inside.`,scenes:[`Say your boss needs to review everything. You feel micromanaged, and you also learn a lot from them.`,`You might be especially motivated to earn a certification because you want a certain mentor to see what you can do.`],advice:`Practice calmly voicing a different opinion to people who carry weight. Respect and independence can exist side by side.`},
'紫微·天府':{title:`Two pillars of support, and two sets of rules`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tian Fu in your Parents palace, the elders and bosses you meet often have real ability and resources and can give you steady support, but their expectations are clear too, with an emphasis on rules and results. You suit large organizations and well-structured environments, and luck with documents and certifications is steady. The lesson: relying too much on your backers, or feeling as if you are always being graded.`,scenes:[`Say you are renting a place or applying for something that needs a guarantor. There is always an elder or former boss willing to step in.`,`Every time you change departments, you might ask around about the new manager's style first so you feel at ease.`],advice:`While you appreciate your backers, also build an ability that doesn't depend on anyone.`},
'紫微·天相':{title:`Elders and bosses who care about appearances`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tian Xiang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses care about image and etiquette and expect a lot from you in manners and rules. You have good luck with documents, contracts and institutions, and suit public service or jobs that require certification. The lesson: caring too much how authority sees you, or getting caught between the expectations of different elders.`,scenes:[`Say it's a holiday family gathering. You are always reminded whom to greet first and what to say to be proper.`,`You might be extra careful with official forms, not wanting a single field wrong.`],advice:`Sort out which rules you truly believe in and which are just habit, and keep only the first kind.`},
'紫微·破軍':{title:`A superior who flips the table and then rebuilds`,story:`With Zi Wei and Po Jun in your Parents palace, your elders or bosses have strong personalities and changeable circumstances, and your relationship with them may have taken clear turns. They taught you how to face change. Your dealings with institutions also shift often, for example through reforms or changes in management. The lesson: you clash easily with authority, and coming to understand each other again takes time.`,scenes:[`Say a new manager reorganizes the team on day one, and you get moved to a project you know nothing about.`,`You might have been distant from an elder when you were young and only come to understand their situation years later.`],advice:`When you disagree with authority, talk about goals first and methods second. Conflict turns into cooperation more easily that way.`},
'紫微·七殺':{title:`A strict, coach-like elder`,story:`With Zi Wei and Qi Sha in your Parents palace, your elders, bosses or teachers are demanding, set high standards, speak bluntly and rarely offer gentle encouragement. From them you learn discipline and resilience, and you are willing to work hard in exams, certifications and competition within the system. The lesson: the pressure is heavy, and you may feel for a long time that you're not good enough.`,scenes:[`Say you hand in a report and your boss only says, "The figures on page three are wrong," without a single word of praise.`,`To earn a certification, you might go to the library every day after work for six months straight.`],advice:`Learn to grade yourself. Don't let a strict voice be the only mirror you have.`},
'紫微·貪狼':{title:`Charming elders with big appetites`,story:`With Zi Wei and Tan Lang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are socially skilled with many interests, and may show you the world and introduce you to many people. The relationship may be warm, or each of you may be busy with your own life. The lesson: their expectations or lifestyle may be very different from yours, and you need to find your own rhythm. Read the terms carefully when you sign documents.`,scenes:[`Say your boss often brings you along to business dinners, and you learn more at the table than in the office.`,`You might have an elder who loves the good life, and that makes you extra careful about saving.`],advice:`Pick the parts of your elders you want to learn from, and politely set the rest aside.`},
'天機':{title:`A clever but changeable mentor`,story:`With Tian Ji in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are smart and quick, and their minds change often. You learn ways of thinking from them, and you may also see your instructions revised again and again. {{B:天機:In a strong position, communication with authority flows well, and your wits help with paperwork and exams.|In a weak position, the relationship changes a lot and you spend more time apart than together.}} The lesson: you can't quite tell what they really want.`,scenes:[`Say your boss wants plan A on Monday and decides B is better on Wednesday, so you just prepare both in advance.`,`You might have moved house or changed schools often as a child, and the adults' job changes shaped you deeply.`],advice:`When you confirm what a superior needs, write it down and send it back. It cuts down on guessing.`},
'天機·太陰':{title:`A thoughtful, sensitive elder`,story:`With Tian Ji and Tai Yin in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are perceptive and caring, but also emotionally sensitive and indirect in how they speak. Your relationship with authority relies on unspoken understanding, and when things aren't said clearly, misunderstandings follow. Planning-oriented work and exams go well for you. The lesson: trying too hard to read their minds.`,scenes:[`Say your boss says, "Think about it some more," and you spend the evening wondering whether they're unhappy.`,`You might rarely share your feelings with a certain elder, yet they always send a message when you are sick.`],advice:`When you're unsure, just ask. Don't let guessing replace communication.`},
'天機·巨門':{title:`A superior who needs a reason for everything`,story:`With Tian Ji and Ju Men in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are articulate and analytical, but they may also be picky and love to argue. You learn logic from them, and you may have grown used to explaining yourself from a young age. Exams in research, law and languages go well, but read the wording of contracts carefully. The lesson: arguments and misunderstandings come easily between you and authority.`,scenes:[`Say your boss grills you on details in a meeting. You prepared three versions of your answer and still get stumped.`,`You might read every clause before signing a contract because you've been burned by fine print before.`],advice:`When you disagree with a superior, let the data do the talking, not your emotions.`},
'天機·天梁':{title:`An elder who acts like a teacher`,story:`With Tian Ji and Tian Liang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses like to guide and advise, often like teachers. You tend to meet mentors willing to teach you, and you suit academia, education, planning and professional certifications. The lesson: there is a lot of advice, so you may feel lectured, or fall into the habit of asking others before you decide.`,scenes:[`Say you are about to change jobs. You call a former teacher first to hear what they think.`,`You might have a boss who loves to explain the principle behind everything. You complain that they go on and on, but you remember what they said.`],advice:`After you hear the advice, the final decision is yours to make, and yours to own.`},
'太陽':{title:`Lighting your way, and heating you up too`,story:`With Tai Yang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are warm-hearted, have a strong sense of justice and care about reputation. They are willing to go to bat for you, and may also take charge of a lot. Traditionally this also points to the influence of male elders. {{B:太陽:In a strong position, help from elders is clear and dealings with institutions go smoothly.|In a weak position, the relationship is harder work, and you carry many things on your own.}} The lesson: the pressure of being expected to shine.`,scenes:[`Say your boss argues for an opportunity for you in a senior meeting, then comes back and insists you deliver results.`,`You might have learned early to look after the people around you, and as an adult you easily take load off your boss.`],advice:`Be grateful to those who light your way, and allow yourself times when you don't shine.`},
'太陽·太陰':{title:`Two kinds of care, one warm and one cool`,story:`With Tai Yang and Tai Yin in your Parents palace, you may have known two styles of elder, one outgoing and direct and one reserved and subtle, or a single elder who runs hot and cold. As a result, you are good at switching between very different personalities. The lesson: adapting between two sets of expectations, and in the end finding your own way.`,scenes:[`Say you have two managers. One wants you to push sales and the other wants you to watch the details, and you go back and forth between them.`,`You might be close to one important elder and distant from another, with a different way of relating to each.`],advice:`You don't need to satisfy everyone at once. Choose one standard you believe in.`},
'太陽·巨門':{title:`An elder who can talk, and loves to`,story:`With Tai Yang and Ju Men in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses speak directly, talk a lot and care about right and wrong. You learn to speak and debate from them, and may also hear a lot of criticism. You suit exams and certifications related to media, teaching, law or foreign languages. The lesson: arguments and misunderstandings build up easily.`,scenes:[`Say there is a family dinner. A certain elder always comments on your job at the table.`,`Before talking with your boss, you might be in the habit of preparing your counterarguments.`],advice:`Treat an elder's criticism as information, not as a verdict on you, and you'll feel much lighter.`},
'太陽·天梁':{title:`A principled guardian who steps in`,story:`With Tai Yang and Tian Liang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are principled and eager to help, often in the role of protector, and you easily come under their wing. Your luck with exams, public service, paperwork and certifications is good, and you suit building a career within the system. The lesson: protection can turn into control, or you get too used to someone shielding you from the storm.`,scenes:[`Say you are preparing for a civil service exam. There's always a senior who lends you their neatly organized notes.`,`You might be a grown adult and still get calls from elders reminding you to look after your health and go to bed early.`],advice:`While you accept protection, practice facing a hard problem on your own.`},
'武曲':{title:`An elder who speaks through actions, not words`,story:`With Wu Qu in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are practical and straightforward, speak directly, and show they care through actions rather than words. There may be some distance in the relationship, and they may have wanted you to be independent early. You handle paperwork and financial matters well. The lesson: communication is stiff, and neither side says much about what they feel.`,scenes:[`Say a certain elder has never said "I'm proud of you," yet quietly paid a year of your insurance premiums.`,`In meetings with your boss, you might only talk numbers and rarely share your thoughts.`],advice:`Try saying a word of thanks or care first. Even a rigid relationship can loosen.`},
'武曲·天府':{title:`A steady backer who knows how to keep money`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tian Fu in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses value financial stability, may support you with resources, and shape you with their views on money. You suit certifications and jobs in finance, accounting and management. The lesson: being pushed to play it safe, or having too much money calculation mixed into the relationship.`,scenes:[`Say you are buying your first home, and an elder hands you a table comparing every bank's mortgage rates.`,`You might have been taught to save since childhood, and now you get nervous for friends who spend freely.`],advice:`Use your elders' money experience as a reference, then decide according to your own life goals.`},
'武曲·天相':{title:`A superior who values rules and responsibility`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tian Xiang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are responsible and trustworthy, and do everything by the book. Your dealings with institutions, paperwork and contracts are stable, and you suit administration, finance and law. The lesson: there are many rules, so you may feel boxed in, or often end up handling practical matters for your elders.`,scenes:[`Say your boss requires a receipt for every expense, not even a cup of coffee excepted.`,`You might be the one in your family who handles all the paperwork, bills and applications.`],advice:`When you take on responsibility, remember to share the load. Don't become the only point of contact.`},
'武曲·七殺':{title:`A stern, direct elder`,story:`With Wu Qu and Qi Sha in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are forceful, blunt and focused on efficiency. There may be tension or distance between you, and you learned early to hold yourself up. You can endure hardship within the system, but you get hurt when you go head to head with authority. The lesson: both sides communicate too rigidly, and neither will back down first.`,scenes:[`Say your boss corrects you in front of everyone. You hold it in at the time, and the more you think about it at home, the angrier you get.`,`You might have started working part-time very young and be used to doing everything yourself.`],advice:`With forceful people, give your feelings a night to settle and talk the next day. The result will be different.`},
'武曲·破軍':{title:`A relationship that has taken big turns`,story:`With Wu Qu and Po Jun in your Parents palace, your elders' or bosses' circumstances may change a lot, for example through financial ups and downs or job changes, and your relationship with them may have gone through separations and reunions, which made you independent early. Read the terms and financial details of documents carefully. The lesson: you don't easily feel safe leaning on authority.`,scenes:[`Say your company reorganizes and the boss who promoted you suddenly leaves, so you have to prove yourself all over again.`,`You might have watched the adults worry about money as a child, so you started saving for yourself especially early.`],advice:`You don't have to repeat your elders' story. The lessons you learned from them are your assets.`},
'武曲·貪狼':{title:`An elder you understand better over time`,story:`With Wu Qu and Tan Lang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are capable and ambitious, and may be busy with their careers or social lives. Early on your relationship with them is fairly distant, and the older you get, the better you understand each other. The lesson: a gap in expectations. You wanted company, and what they gave may have been resources.`,scenes:[`Say the adults were often away when you were small, and only as a grown-up did you realize how hard they were working.`,`You might have worked for a boss with real business sense and picked up the finer points of making money from them.`],advice:`Look at your elders again as an adult. Some regrets you can let go, and some experience you can keep.`},
'天同':{title:`A gentle elder who never pushes`,story:`With Tian Tong in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are mild and easy to get along with and don't put much pressure on you, so your relationship with authority is fairly relaxed. {{B:天同:In a strong position, you receive plenty of care.|In a weak position, they may want to help but lack the means, so you need to find your own way more often.}} The lesson: a comfortable environment gives you less of a push, and you tend to put off exams and certifications.`,scenes:[`Say your boss rarely chases deadlines, so you have to set your own.`,`You might sign up for a certification exam and keep postponing it because no one is pushing you.`],advice:`Find someone to keep pace with you. A comfortable environment can still have momentum.`},
'天同·太陰':{title:`A soft, attentive caregiver`,story:`With Tian Tong and Tai Yin in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are gentle and attentive and take care of you emotionally, and women elders may have a deeper influence on you. Your relationship with authority leans toward warmth. The lesson: emotional ties, or elders who are emotionally sensitive and need you to spend effort reassuring them.`,scenes:[`Say you are changing jobs, and your first worry is whether a certain elder will be upset.`,`You might have a female manager who notices you look tired lately and asks if you'd like to leave early.`],advice:`Before you take care of other people's feelings, make sure your own have somewhere to go.`},
'天同·巨門':{title:`Close, yet often unable to say things clearly`,story:`With Tian Tong and Ju Men in your Parents palace, there may be a communication gap between you and your elders and bosses: friendly on the surface, with each side quietly feeling wronged. Watch the details on paperwork, and don't fully trust verbal promises. The lesson: things go unsaid, and misunderstandings build up bit by bit.`,scenes:[`Say an elder says "Do whatever you want," and you can't tell whether that means yes or that they are annoyed.`,`You might have had a boss promise you a raise in conversation, then claim six months later not to remember it.`],advice:`Write down important agreements, and when you don't understand something, ask once directly.`},
'天同·天梁':{title:`A blessed knack for meeting helpful people`,story:`With Tian Tong and Tian Liang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are kind and willing to look after you, and at key moments you often get help from mentors or teachers. You suit charity, education, healthcare and service work. The lesson: relying too much on protection and lacking experience in making your own decisions.`,scenes:[`Say you have just started working, and a senior colleague spends a whole afternoon teaching you how to build a report.`,`When you hit a problem, your first thought might be "Let me go ask my teacher."`],advice:`Pass on the care you've received, and you will gradually become a helpful person in someone else's life.`},
'廉貞':{title:`A superior with strict rules and a strong personality`,story:`With Lian Zhen in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are principled and distinctive, care about rules and boundaries, and your relationship with authority may involve some push and pull that takes time to work out. When you deal with institutions, paperwork and official matters, follow the rules and don't skimp on details. The lesson: swinging between respect and rebellion.`,scenes:[`Say your boss is big on process. Whenever you want to simplify a step, you have to write a report explaining why.`,`You might often disagree with a certain elder, yet still want to hear their view at the key moments.`],advice:`Find rules you both agree on, and there will be less tug-of-war.`},
'廉貞·天府':{title:`A rule-abiding keeper of the treasury`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tian Fu in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are steady, rule-minded and attentive to finances, and give you solid support. Your dealings with institutions and paperwork are stable, and you suit administration, management and finance. The lesson: conservative views can hold you back, or you are both so polite that little is said from the heart.`,scenes:[`Say an elder keeps reminding you to get insurance and to check your social insurance records.`,`You might work for a boss with a steady style and learn from them how to control costs.`],advice:`On that stable foundation, also let your elders know what you want to try.`},
'廉貞·天相':{title:`A system that values titles and etiquette`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tian Xiang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses care about rules and proper roles, and you easily earn trust within the system. Paperwork, contracts, law, administration and certifications go well for you. The lesson: you often mediate between different elders, or their expectations put a lot of pressure on you.`,scenes:[`Say your company holds an event, and your boss hands you all the formal invitations to outside guests.`,`You might be the one in your family who helps settle disputes between the older relatives.`],advice:`When you mediate, be clear about what you can and can't do. You don't need to take responsibility for everyone's feelings.`},
'廉貞·七殺':{title:`Some distance makes peace possible`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Qi Sha in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are forceful with high standards, and being around them brings pressure and friction. You build toughness from it, and you may also want to escape their control early on. When dealing with institutions, follow the rules and avoid impulsive confrontations. The lesson: using force to deal with authority.`,scenes:[`Say you and your boss have one big argument over how to do things, and afterward you actually respect each other.`,`You might have badly wanted to move out when you were young, and only after you did move did things with your elders slowly ease.`],advice:`Keep a healthy distance, and the relationship will have room to heal.`},
'廉貞·破軍':{title:`Learning to grow up on your own amid change`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Po Jun in your Parents palace, your elders' or bosses' circumstances, or your relationship with them, may go through big changes, such as new managers, policy changes or changes in the family. Because of this you learned early to adapt. Watch for changed terms in documents. The lesson: a sense of distrust toward authority.`,scenes:[`Say a company you worked at had four managers in three years, and you learned not to depend on any one person.`,`You might have been through changes at home as a child and become independent earlier than your peers.`],advice:`You can choose which elders to trust. You don't have to accept everything, and you don't have to reject everything either.`},
'廉貞·貪狼':{title:`Colorful, changeable elders`,story:`With Lian Zhen and Tan Lang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are widely connected, have many interests and vivid personalities. They are charming, and they may also leave you feeling things aren't stable enough. You learn social skills from them. The lesson: their lifestyle differs from your values, so you need to draw boundaries. Watch the details when you sign documents.`,scenes:[`Say your boss loves socializing and often calls you at the last minute to help out at a dinner party.`,`You might have an elder who loves a crowd and loves to spend, and you end up being the calmest person around.`],advice:`Respect your elders' way of life, and hold on to your own boundaries.`},
'天府':{title:`A solid backer standing behind you`,story:`With Tian Fu in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are steady and well resourced, and willing to support you in practical ways. Your dealings with institutions, paperwork and certifications usually go smoothly. The lesson: conservative expectations make you afraid to take risks, or you get used to someone else catching you if you fall.`,scenes:[`Say you are about to change jobs, and your former boss offers, "If you need a reference letter, I'll write one."`,`Every time you face a big decision, you might first listen to what a trusted elder has to say.`],advice:`Be grateful for your backers, and in your own field build the kind of ability others can lean on.`},
'太陰':{title:`Quiet care that goes unspoken`,story:`With Tai Yin in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are gentle and attentive, and their care often goes unspoken. Traditionally this also points to the influence of female elders. {{B:太陰:In a strong position, their care is attentive and their support steady.|In a weak position, there may be less care from them, or more distance between you.}} The lesson: feelings are held back, and though you care about each other, you rarely say so.`,scenes:[`Say a certain elder doesn't talk much, but always makes your favorite dish when you visit.`,`You might have a boss who never praises you face to face, yet gives you the top score in your annual review.`],advice:`Try saying one caring sentence first. Even reserved relationships need someone to speak up.`},
'貪狼':{title:`A multi-talented, busy elder`,story:`With Tan Lang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses have wide interests and busy social lives. They may introduce you to many new things, and they may also be too busy to look after you much. The lesson: a gap between expectations and time together. With exams and certifications, your many interests make it easy to get distracted.`,scenes:[`Say your boss brings you to all kinds of exhibitions and gatherings, and you meet a lot of people that way.`,`You might want to earn several certifications at once and end up studying only half of each.`],advice:`Prepare for one goal at a time. That's how your talents add up to results.`},
'巨門':{title:`A relationship with things left unsaid`,story:`With Ju Men in your Parents palace, there tend to be communication gaps or disagreements between you and your elders and bosses, or things each side has never said out loud. {{B:巨門:In a strong position, they may influence you through their expertise and way with words.|In a weak position, there are more misunderstandings and arguments.}} Read documents and contracts carefully. The lesson: unresolved knots build up.`,scenes:[`Say an elder makes an offhand comment, and you remember it for years.`,`When talking with your boss, you might often feel that what you said and what they heard are two different things.`],advice:`Say what matters to you directly. Clearing the air once beats years of guessing.`},
'天相':{title:`A dependable system and superiors`,story:`With Tian Xiang in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses are fair and trustworthy, and within the system you easily earn trust and care. Your luck with paperwork, certifications and contracts is good, and you suit administration, law and management. The lesson: caring too much about your superiors' opinion, or being handed too many small chores.`,scenes:[`Say you are filing all kinds of applications and documents, and the process always goes surprisingly smoothly.`,`Colleagues might see you as the one the boss trusts most, which is also why the odd jobs always land on you.`],advice:`Beyond being dependable, let your superiors know where you want to grow.`},
'天梁':{title:`Born with an elder's umbrella`,story:`Tian Liang is the star of shelter. In your Parents palace, elders, bosses and teachers easily become your umbrella. Exams, certifications, public service, healthcare and education all go well for you. The lesson: they may take charge of too much and like to lecture, or you depend so much on protection that you have little experience facing things alone.`,scenes:[`Say a teacher always took special care of you at school and recommended you for competitions.`,`You might be thirty and still have an elder calling to remind you to dress warmly when it's cold.`],advice:`Treat protection as a starting point, not the destination, and slowly learn to hold your own umbrella.`},
'七殺':{title:`An elder who made you grow up early`,story:`With Qi Sha in your Parents palace, your elders and bosses have strong personalities and high demands, the relationship may carry distance or pressure, and you learned to be independent early. Within the system you don't like being managed, yet you deliver results under high pressure. The lesson: you always keep your guard up around authority.`,scenes:[`Say your first job came with an extremely strict boss, and that is exactly where you built your most solid skills.`,`You might rarely ask your elders for help, used to figuring things out yourself.`],advice:`You've already proven you can do it alone. Now you can practice letting people help a little.`},
'破軍':{title:`A bond that can be torn up and rewritten`,story:`With Po Jun in your Parents palace, your relationship with elders and bosses may have gone through changes, distance or fresh starts, you often get new managers or teachers, and you tend to challenge established systems. The lesson: authority doesn't give you a sense of security, so you always want to do things yourself.`,scenes:[`Say a new boss takes over and your old way of working is scrapped and rebuilt from scratch.`,`You might have lost touch with an elder and only started talking again years later at some occasion.`],advice:`Use your present-day perspective to decide how close to stay to each elder.`},
'空':{title:`Relationships with elders lit by borrowed light`,story:`Your Parents palace has no main star, so your relationships with elders, bosses and institutions are flexible and strongly shaped by circumstances; the chart borrows the main stars of the opposite palace for reference. At different stages you may meet mentors with completely different styles, and some of those roles may be missing altogether. The upside is that you can learn from all kinds of people; the lesson is that without a fixed support, you need to build your own inner standards.`,scenes:[`Say you have had three jobs with three bosses of completely different styles, and you adjusted every time.`,`You might not have one steady mentor, and instead piece together your own approach from books, online courses and different seniors.`],advice:`Choose a few role models you want to learn from. They don't have to be family; they can be anyone you admire.`}
}
});
